{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"The multi-voter configuration loss reproduces (mode on: index 1 with 3 servers; control: index 14 with 5), but the minority-election consequence did not emerge in the probe. Let me submit the witnessed part and record the negative honestly."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['rationale']=(\\\"The multi-voter variant that question-0 listed as unwitnessed is now built and probed. A three-voter cluster takes one deliberate snapshot (automatic snapshots disabled so nothing newer can cover the change), grows to five voters, and the leader is restarted from its own stores: with RestoreCommittedLogs on it comes back holding the snapshot's three-voter configuration at index 1 while its own log's latest configuration is index 14 with five servers; without the flag the same restart keeps index 14 with five servers. That addresses the single-voter limitation with a real membership change, not just a bootstrap entry. A second consequence was attempted in the same harness: after restarting, the node is partitioned together with one committed voter so that the remaining three voters hold a majority of the committed five-voter configuration while the restarted node believes the quorum is two. In the probe the restarted node did not campaign to leadership (became_leader false in both modes) although the majority side did keep a leader, so that consequence is recorded as an attempted discrimination that did not emerge rather than as a claim; only the configuration comparison is declared. Nothing else is restated.\\\")\nd['sources']=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":604,\\\"end_line\\\":620,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":724,\\\"end_line\\\":754,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":655,\\\"end_line\\\":681,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":994,\\\"end_line\\\":1005,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_follower_election_abort\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":228,\\\"end_line\\\":246,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1087,\\\"end_line\\\":1094,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"config_restore_committed_doc\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"config.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":242,\\\"end_line\\\":254,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"log_commit_tracking_iface\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"log.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":194,\\\"end_line\\\":219,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"interface_statement\\\"}\n]\nd['investigations']=[\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@multivoter\\\",\\\"parent_id\\\":\\\"ef5ddbf78bd4456ea51537bd60a60a80-question-0\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Does the configuration loss also occur for a real membership change in a multi-voter cluster, and can the resulting stale membership produce a decision the committed configuration would not allow?\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"raft_follower_election_abort\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\"],\n  \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"A node restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs keeps the snapshot's configuration when committed membership changes sit below the restored commit index, so its quorum arithmetic reflects an obsolete membership.\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Grow a snapshot-age three-voter cluster to five voters, restart the leader, and compare the configuration index and server count with the log's latest configuration; then isolate the restarted node with one committed voter and see whether it can win with its smaller quorum.\\\"}\n]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('stage1 ok')\nPYEOF\necho done\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
