{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nfor q in d.get('investigations',[]):\n    if q.get('ref')=='@multivoter':\n        q['parent_id']='ef5ddbf78bd4456ea51537bd60a61a80-question-0'\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@multivoter\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"api_addvoter\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Boot three voters with RestoreCommittedLogs and CommitTrackingLogs, disable automatic snapshots and take exactly one snapshot while the configuration is still the bootstrap one, add two further voters so the committed configuration has five servers, commit more entries, then restart the node that was leading from its own stores and compare the configuration it holds with the log's latest configuration. Run the same sequence with the flag on and off.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The single deliberate snapshot carries only the bootstrap configuration, so it cannot represent the later membership change.\\\",\\\"Automatic snapshots are disabled, so no newer snapshot can cover the change.\\\",\\\"Adding the two voters commits because the leader still has a majority of the committed configuration.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Whole-package or repository test suites.\\\",\\\"Any claim about an election won with the stale quorum; the partition stage of the harness is exploratory and produced no such leader.\\\",\\\"The other two questions, unchanged here.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"voters_before\\\":3,\\\"voters_after\\\":5,\\\"snapshots\\\":1,\\\"restarted_node\\\":\\\"leader\\\"}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness uses the package's own test facilities: MakeClusterCustom with Peers 3, CommitTrackingLogs and RestoreCommittedLogs; ten Apply calls; an explicit Snapshot(); MakeClusterNoBootstrap(2) merged with FullyConnect and two AddVoter calls; ten further Apply calls; then Shutdown and NewRaft on the same logs, stable and snapshots stores with a fresh inmem transport, followed by FullConnect on the rewired transports. It emits a startup_before_restart event carrying the snapshot index, the snapshot's configuration index, the expected configuration index and server count, then a multivoter_after_restart event with the configuration observed after NewRaft returns and the operand of the comparison.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The library owns the membership view a node resumes with; a caller that enables RestoreCommittedLogs still expects the committed configuration in the node's own log to govern its quorum arithmetic.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"mv_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"mv_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"mv_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"mv_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"multivoter_after_restart\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"mv_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"config_matches\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After restarting from a log whose latest configuration has five servers while the snapshot carries three, the node's configuration index and server count are expected to match the log; the defect prediction is that it falls back to the snapshot's configuration.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"multivoter_after_restart\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"mv_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"config_matches\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the identical restart without the flag is expected to keep the five-server configuration, isolating the recovery path rather than the restart and the membership change.\\\"}]}\nd['interpretations']=[\n {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@multivoter\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\"],\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"conditional\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Source: the same mechanism as the parent question applies to a real membership change, not just to a bootstrap entry: restoreFromCommittedLogs (api.go:724-754) sets lastApplied to the persisted commit index before the scan at api.go:604-620, restoreSnapshot (api.go:655-681) can only supply the snapshot's configuration, and AddVoter (api.go:994-1005) writes a later LogConfiguration that is only re-read if it sits above the restored commit index. A native construction probe reproduced the predicted difference with five committed voters: with the flag on the restarted leader came back with after_latest_index 1 and after_servers 3 (the snapshot's bootstrap configuration) against expected_latest_index 14 and expected_servers 5, while the flag-off control came back with index 14 and five servers; in the same probe the pre-restart state was index 14 with five servers in both modes, so the change itself committed in both. A second consequence was attempted and did not emerge: after the restart the node was partitioned together with one committed voter while the remaining three voters kept a majority of the committed five-voter configuration, and the restarted node never reached Leader in either mode (became_leader false, majority_side_leader true, reachable_votes 2 against committed_quorum 3), so an election won with a minority of the committed configuration is not claimed. Only the configuration comparison is declared, and only its receipt can make it complete.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The flag-off control keeps the five-server configuration through the same membership change and restart, isolating the flagged recovery path.\\\",\\\"The attempted minority-election consequence did not emerge in the probe: the restarted node stayed out of leadership in both modes, so the safety consequence beyond the lost configuration remains unestablished.\\\"],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"No receipt yet for the multi-voter scenario; the account rests on source reading plus a native probe.\\\",\\\"The minority-election consequence is explicitly not claimed; the partition stage is retained as an exploratory negative with its operands.\\\",\\\"The probe used the in-memory commit-tracking store and a single deliberate snapshot; other snapshot timings are not explored.\\\"]}\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('stage2 ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
